course: dictionary
lesson: 5148
title: Irish: a describing word or a naming word?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word Irish can work in two ways. It can describe something, as in «Irish dancing», which tells you the dancing comes from Ireland. It can also name something, as in «the Irish language», where Irish is the language itself. To tell which, look at the words around it and ask: is Irish telling me what kind of thing this is, or is it the name of the thing?
explain: Context helps again. «Irish children learn both English and Irish at school.» Children learn a language, not a country, so the second Irish must be a naming word for the language. In «Irish stew», Irish describes the stew: it is a stew from Ireland.
explain: Ireland is an island west of Great Britain, with the Irish Sea between them. Most of the island is the Republic of Ireland. The north is Northern Ireland, which is part of the UK. So Irish can mean something from the whole island, even though the two parts have different governments.
fact: Irish can be an adjective, a describing word: «Irish dancing» is dancing from Ireland.
fact: Irish can also be a noun, a naming word: «the Irish language» is also called Gaeilge.
fact: «The Irish» means the people of Ireland.
fact: Ireland is an island west of Great Britain.
fact: «Eejit» is Irish slang for a fool, and «sap» means a softie.
exercise: In «Irish stew», what does Irish tell you? | *It comes from Ireland | It means the people | It is a very cold food | It is the name of a language
exercise: «Irish children learn both English and Irish at school.» What is Irish in this sentence? | *The language | A country on the map | A kind of dance | A fool
exercise: Where is Ireland on the map? | *West of Great Britain, as an island | In the middle of Africa | East of Spain, on the mainland | Under the Irish Sea, hidden
test: In «Irish monks made beautiful books such as the Book of Kells», what does Irish describe? | The colour of the books | A language spoken in Scotland | A football game | *Monks from Ireland
test: Which sentence describes the Irish Sea? | The sea around Australia | A sea in the middle of Africa | *The sea between Ireland and Great Britain | A lake in the middle of Scotland
exam: Tadhg says, «I am learning Irish at school.» What is Irish here? | A dance | *The language | A county | The sea
